{"type": "_fixture_provenance", "note": "Synthesized 2026-09-12 and extended 2026-10-03; no real transcript was copied. The frames a turn that fans out to subagents writes, measured on claude 2.1.269 with `-p --input-format stream-json --output-format stream-json --verbose --permission-mode default --permission-prompt-tool stdio` against two parallel Agent calls: every line one of those subagents writes carries parent_tool_use_id at the top of the envelope and the parent's own carry null; system/task_started is the one frame binding the CLI's own handle for a subagent (task_id) to the call that launched it (tool_use_id), and it carries description and subagent_type; a can_use_tool raised inside a subagent's run names that handle as agent_id and never the launching call, which is why the adapter keeps the pair. The task frames take the fields and order a 2.1.288 run with --forward-subagent-text printed (2026-10-03, one Haiku subagent counting with Bash): task_started adds is_backgrounded, spawn_depth, task_type local_agent and prompt; task_progress comes once per tool call; task_updated carries patch.status; task_notification carries status, summary and usage. Subagent B ends the way a stop_task kill ends one in the 2.1.288 binary, task_updated killed and then task_notification stopped. Session id, tool_use ids and agent handles are invented; field names, nesting and ordering are the measured ones, and the two subagents write the same sentence because that is the case the grouping has to tell apart."}
